  "observation": "Orphaned workspace placement now anchors to the destination output origin and wraps negative logical coordinates without changing size. The observed returning floating application retains workspace 2 and its unsaved draft, is reachable at x=40/y=230, activates through the actual taskbar exactly once, receives GTK press plus client-wire release and physical keyboard editing, and paints onscreen. Original two-output move/resize/cancel/capture and unchanged MAX/snap caption/lifecycle regression pass one native tuple with normal cleanup.",
  "missingObservations": [
    "Independent original UI-019 scenario review, physical output hotplug and native AT/IME remain open.",
    "Native negative/nonzero destination origin, smaller/rotated/scaled outputs and minimized/pinned/fullscreen/modal recovery remain unqualified. Existing-monitor translation still preserves relative placement; this fix does not establish arbitrary smaller-output fit. Original vertical partial clipping is unchanged.",
    "Fresh old native shortcut receipts delayed across identical replacement bounds and arbitrary host/native generation ordering remain unqualified; the source/retirement abstractions are atomic.",
    "Pending preview/capture/effect custody, protected input, Unknown reconciliation, transport EAGAIN/backpressure and fatal parent-loss runtime schedules remain unqualified.",
    "Full original release journeys, measured hardware/resource budgets, reproducible package and reversible deployment remain open."
  ],
