  "probeCorrections": [
    "A preflight refused the new owning TU until its exact two changed-source paths were admitted. A second preflight hit the 12-node ancestry bound; bounded hash/cycle validation now allows 64 nodes. Neither launched a GUI or changed original observation deadlines.",
    "The unchanged GTK window GestureClick observer records an editor press but not its gesture-level release. The client Wayland trace independently shows press/release on the same pointer proxy with no intervening enter/leave.",
    "The attempted raw Gtk.EventControllerLegacy observer received None for its event through PyGObject and raised AttributeError; its failed packet/log is retained, and this observer was removed. The final proof uses existing native client wire events plus named GTK press and actual edited text.",
    "A fresh 800x600 virtual-pointer helper sends the actual returned-output click; the retained drag device has its original 1600x600 absolute extent and is unchanged."
  ],
